  "result": "I wrote the 30-minute lesson on context and memory, plus a short quiz and a cheat sheet. I haven't opened the lesson in a browser or run any checks on the files.\n\n- **Lesson:** `lessons/0001-context-and-memory-in-an-agent.html` (objective O3). You finish able to sort each piece of information in the makerspace assistant into one of four places: the context window, a saved note, a live tool call, or a searched library. The sections are:\n  - the context window\n  - what carries over between steps, with a worked token count\n  - why more context isn't better (context rot)\n  - notes as memory between sessions\n  - retrieval of manual pages\n  - a worked example and a practice task using the assistant\n\n  Each section has a practice check with instant feedback. I estimate the length at roughly 3,500 words, which should land between 23 and 25 minutes of reading plus the exercises.\n- **Quiz:** `quizzes/0002.json`, five items on the lesson's ideas, with the key in `keys/0002.json`. It's ready when you want it.\n- **Cheat sheet:** `cheatsheets/context-and-memory.html`, a one-page \"where does it go?\" reference.\n- **Other files:** `RESOURCES.md` (new) and `NOTES.md` (updated).\n\nThe lesson draws on Anthropic's article on context engineering and its docs on context windows and the memory tool, which I read in full. I couldn't find a good beginner source on embeddings and chunking, so the lesson keeps that part light and `RESOURCES.md` lists it as a gap.\n\nAsk me anything about the lesson. One question for you: do you want a follow-up on compaction and sub-agents, which the lesson only mentions, or should the next lesson be tool descriptions?",
